README was improved.

commit abcdef0123456789abcdef0123456789
Author: Homer Simpson <simpson@burns-powerplant.com>
Date: Sun Dec 31 09:12:34 2001 +0100

initial commit

$ git gq applied
abcdef0 script.sh was improved.
abcdef0 README was improved.

$ git gq unapplied

-------------------------------------------------
do backup, then modifiy patches
-------------------------------------------------


$ git backup
hint: Using 'master' as the name for the initial branch. This default branch name
hint: is subject to change. To configure the initial branch name to use in all
hint: of your new repositories, which will suppress this warning, call:
hint:
hint: 	git config --global init.defaultBranch <name>
hint:
hint: Names commonly chosen instead of 'master' are 'main', 'trunk' and
hint: 'development'. The just-created branch can be renamed via this command:
hint:
hint: 	git branch -m <name>
Initialized empty Git repository in /.gqpatches/.git/
[master (root-commit) abcdef0] backup 2001-12-31T091234
4 files changed, 43 insertions(+)
create mode 100644 default/applied/0001-README-was-improved.patch
create mode 100644 default/applied/0002-script.sh-was-improved.patch
create mode 100644 default/parent
create mode 100644 queue
.gqpatches/default/applied/0001-README-was-improved.patch
.gqpatches/default/applied/0002-script.sh-was-improved.patch
$ git gq pop -a
HEAD is now at abcdef0 README was improved.
HEAD is now at abcdef0 initial commit

# Invert order of patches

$ git gq push -a
Checking patch script.sh...
Applied patch script.sh cleanly.
Applying: script.sh was improved.
Checking patch README.txt...
Applied patch README.txt cleanly.
Applying: README was improved.

# Change README.txt again ...
$ git gq new README-was-extended
[master abcdef0] README-was-extended
1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)
$ git gq pop
HEAD is now at abcdef0 README was improved.

$ git gq applied
abcdef0 README was improved.
abcdef0 script.sh was improved.

$ git gq unapplied
README-was-extended.patch

-------------------------------------------------
restore patches
-------------------------------------------------


Now restore.
$git gq restore HEAD
Note: switching to 'abcdef0'.

You are in 'detached HEAD' state. You can look around, make experimental
changes and commit them, and you can discard any commits you make in this
state without impacting any branches by switching back to a branch.

If you want to create a new branch to retain commits you create, you may
do so (now or later) by using -c with the switch command. Example:

git switch -c <new-branch-name>

Or undo this operation with:

git switch -

Turn off this advice by setting config variable advice.detachedHead to false

HEAD is now at abcdef0 backup 2001-12-31T091234
Removing default/README-was-extended.patch
Removing default/series
Removing tmp/
You can now re-create the patch queue with 'git gq revert'.

Now revert.
$git gq revert
Reverting changes in repository cannot be undone easily.
Continue ?
Enter 'y' or 'Y' to continue, everything else aborts.Applying: README was improved.
Applying: script.sh was improved.

